+# core/data/talk/grammar/en/ask_topic.tlk - T5b: more replies to ASK_ABOUT(x) and
+# ASK_OPINION(x), the two question acts that carry a topic (owner: TK; the starter lines
+# are in core_ask.tlk; syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py; register: SCRIPT_STYLE.md).
+#
+# How the topic is written here, so one template reads right for a food, a job, a place,
+# a person and a mass noun:
+#   "{x:cap}?"            the echo of the player's word: any topic
+#   {x:pl}                the generic form ("pies", "butter", "dancing", "Nana Puddin"):
+#                         only with verbs that do not agree (past tense, can, "made")
+#   {x:def} {x.is}        "the pie is", "the slippers are", "Nana Puddin is"
+#   {x.it}                it / they, after an echo
+# A template that needs a count noun says needs: x.countable. Everything here is kid-safe.
+
+# ---- the verdict sub-rules (one short sentence each; they follow an echo) ---------------
+@rule ask.star.pro
+  "Five stars."
+  "Ten out of ten."
+  "Cozy grade: A."
+  "Gold sticker."
+  "Top shelf."
+  "Two thumbs up."
+  "Blue ribbon."
+@rule ask.star.con
+  "One star."
+  "Zero out of ten."
+  "Cozy grade: F."
+  "No sticker."
+  "Bottom shelf."
+  "Two thumbs down."
+@rule ask.star.mid
+  "Three stars."
+  "Five out of ten."
+  "Cozy grade: C."
+  "A firm shrug."
+  "Middle shelf."
+  "One thumb, sideways."
+
+# ---- ASK_ABOUT(x), by stance ---------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_about.pro2 guard: stance=pro act: opine_pos
+  "{x:pl:cap} got me through a bad winter. I still send a card."
+  "{x:cap}? Sit down. This takes a while and I have slides."
+  "I'd put {x:pl} on the town flag. Right over the turkey."
+  "{x:cap}? Best thing since the save point."
+  "Ask me about {x:pl} again. Slower. I want to enjoy it."
+  "{x:def:cap} {x.is} {x.good}, and I'll say so at the town meeting."
+  "{x:cap}? My happy meter just went up. I felt it click."
+  "If loving {x:pl} is wrong, I'm wrong. Loudly. Daily."
+  "{x:cap}? {ask.star.pro} I checked twice."
+  "I'd trade a whole cake for {x:indef}. A small cake. Still."
+  "I keep a list of good things. {x:pl:cap} made the list. In pen."
+  "{x:cap}? {x.good:cap}. Like {x.assoc:indef}, but more so."
+  "You said {x} and my whole day got better. Say it again."
+  "{x:cap}? {ask.star.pro} And I'm a tough crowd."
+@rule core.ask_about.con2 guard: stance=con act: opine_neg
+  "{x:cap}? {ask.star.con} And I'm being kind."
+  "Me and {x:pl} had a falling out. I started it. I'd do it again."
+  "{x:cap}? My happy meter just dipped. You did that."
+  "I keep a list of things to avoid. {x:pl:cap} made the top three."
+  "{x:def:cap} {x.is} {x.bad}. I don't make the rules. I'd make worse ones."
+  "{x:cap}? Oh no. Who let {x.it} in?"
+  "You want my honest answer on {x:pl}? Get a helmet."
+  "{x:cap}? I'd cross the street. Then I'd cross another street."
+  "I tried to like {x:pl}. I gave it a whole afternoon."
+  "{x:cap}. Hm. Is there a form to un-hear that?"
+  "{x:cap}? Needs salt. Needs a lot more than salt."
+  "{x:cap}? {ask.star.con} I'd go lower, but the scale stops."
+  "I don't trust {x:pl}. I trust the fog more, and the fog lies."
+@rule core.ask_about.neutral2 guard: stance=neutral act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? {ask.star.mid} That's my whole review."
+  "{x:def:cap} {x.is} {x.adj}. I read that on a sign."
+  "I know two things about {x:pl}. Both are wrong."
+  "{x:cap}? I never think about {x.it}. Now I am, thanks to you."
+  "{x:pl:cap} happened to me once. I got over it."
+  "{x:cap}? Goes with {x.assoc:pl}, right? Don't quote me."
+  "What about {x:pl}? You brought it up. You go first."
+  "{x:cap}? I can take {x.it} or leave {x.it}. Mostly I leave {x.it}."
+  "There's a pamphlet on {x:pl} at Town Hall. Nobody's read it."
+  "{x:cap}, right. I had an opinion on that. It's in my other coat."
+  "Honestly? I filed {x:pl} under 'later'. It's a big folder."
+  "{x:cap}? I'm told {x.it} {x.is} {x.adj}. I'm told a lot of things."
+  "{x:cap}? {ask.star.mid} Ask me again when I've eaten."
+
+# ---- ASK_ABOUT(x): a story, a joke, a pass, a new subject ----------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_about.story guard: topic act: tell
+  "I saw {x:indef} at the Boneyard Buffet once. Not on the menu."
+  "My nana had a saying about {x:pl}. It was mostly coughing."
+  "Last time {x:pl} came up, the Mayor hid under a tablecloth."
+  "I wrote a poem about {x:pl}. Six lines. Needs salt."
+  "There's a Bandstand Tape about {x:pl}. It's a cooking segment."
+  "{x:cap} reminds me of {x.assoc:pl}. Everything does, lately."
+  "I had a dream about {x:pl}. You were there. You were a lamp."
+  "{x:cap}? Long story. {.}Short version: I was right."
+  "We voted on {x:pl} at the town meeting. It was a tie. Then a fire."
+@rule core.ask_about.joke guard: topic act: joke
+  "{x:cap}? In this economy? In this fog?"
+  "Fun fact about {x:pl}: I don't have one. Fun, right?"
+  "{x:cap}? Never heard of {x.it}. {.}Kidding, I've heard of everything."
+  "You know what they say about {x:pl}. {.}I don't. I hoped you did."
+  "{x:cap}? There's a quest for that. The reward is more {x}." needs: x.mass
+  "{x:indef:cap} walks into a room. This room. That's the joke, hi." needs: x.countable
+  "I'd tell you about {x:pl}, but then it'd be a tutorial."
+@rule core.ask_about.pass guard: topic act: dismiss
+  "{x:cap}? Not today. I've got a nap booked."
+  "Ask me about {x:pl} tomorrow. I'll be out."
+  "No {x} talk before lunch. House rule."
+  "{x:cap}? Pass. I'm saving my words for something good."
+  "That's a question for somebody smarter. Or taller."
+@rule core.ask_about.swerve act: change_topic
+  "Never mind that. Let's do {like:pl}. I've got a whole speech."
+  "That reminds me of {like:pl}. Everything reminds me of {like:pl}."
+  "Good question. Better question: {like:pl}. Go."
+  "I'll answer that right after we cover {like:pl}. So, never."
+
+# ---- ASK_ABOUT(x), by what the topic is -----------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_about.people guard: root=people act: answer
+  "{x:indef:cap}? I know one. Nice enough, but still has my ladder." needs: x.countable
+  "Every town needs {x:indef}. Ours has a few. One waves too much." needs: x.countable
+  "{x:cap}? Good people. Loud at parties, but good people."
+  "I was {x:indef} for one whole day once. I got a certificate." needs: x.countable
+@rule core.ask_about.places guard: root=places act: answer
+  "{x:def:cap}? I go there to think. Then I stop and get a snack."
+  "{x:def:cap} {x.is} nice this time of year. This time of year is fog."
+  "I got lost near {x:def} once. Found a duck. Kept walking."
+  "{x:def:cap}? Cozy grade: B. Loses points for the smell."
+  "They want to put a gift shop in {x:def}. Another one."
+@rule core.ask_about.food2 guard: root=food act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? I have a recipe. Step one is buying {x.it}."
+  "{x:cap} for breakfast, {x} for dinner. Lunch is a mystery."
+  "Nana hides things in {x:pl}. Keys, mostly. Once, a map."
+  "{x:cap}? My hunger meter just blinked. Now look what you did."
+  "Grumbleguts gave {x} a six. He gives everything a six."
+@rule core.ask_about.music guard: root=music act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? I can't sit still for {x.it}. I tapped through a town meeting."
+  "{x:cap}? Bonejangles does it better. On his own ribs."
+  "{x:cap} gets stuck in my head. It's crowded in there already."
+  "I know {x}. Well, the first bit. Then I hum with confidence."
+@rule core.ask_about.hobbies guard: root=hobbies act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? I tried {x.it} once and pulled something. Not mine."
+  "{x:cap} {x.is} how I relax. I'm bad at it. That's the relaxing part."
+  "I'd do more {x} if I had the time. I have the time. I nap." needs: x.gerund
+  "There's a club for {x}. Two members. They aren't speaking."
+  "I took up {x} last spring. {x:cap} put me down again by summer."
+@rule core.ask_about.creatures guard: root=creatures act: answer
+  "{x:indef:cap} lives under my porch. We have an understanding." needs: x.countable
+  "{x:pl:cap}? Cute until they look at you. Then still cute, that's the trap." needs: x.countable
+  "I named {x:indef} once. It didn't answer. Rude." needs: x.countable
+  "{x:pl:cap} know something. I can't prove it. They can." needs: x.countable
+  "{x:cap}? I saw one. It saw me first, and we agreed to say nothing."
+@rule core.ask_about.work guard: root=work act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? That sounds like work. I just sat down."
+  "{x:cap}? It's on my to-do list. The list is lost."
+  "{x:indef:cap}? Honest work. I'd be terrible at it." needs: x.person
+  "We had {x:indef} in town once. Left for the city. The city sent a note." needs: x.person
+  "{x:cap}? I have a meter for that. It's empty, it's always empty."
+@rule core.ask_about.time guard: root=time act: answer
+  "{x:cap}, already? I had plans. Well, I had a plan."
+  "{x:cap}? I lose track. My calendar is a drawing of a duck."
+  "{x:cap} comes around too fast. I blame the fog."
+  "I do my worrying around {x}. I'm fully booked."
+@rule core.ask_about.school guard: root=school act: answer
+  "I got a gold star for {x}. It fell off. I kept the glue."
+  "{x:cap}. I still have the dream where I forgot my shoes."
+  "I learned one thing about {x}. It was 'don't lick the flagpole'."
+  "{x:cap}? Miss Lulla covers that. Twice, for the ones at the back."
+@rule core.ask_about.feelings guard: root=feelings act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? I had that on Tuesday, all day. It passed."
+  "{x:cap} {x.is} a meter I don't have. I checked the menu."
+  "{x:cap}? Father Fuzz says hug it out. He says that about soup."
+  "I keep {x} in a drawer. Under the good spoons."
+@rule core.ask_about.stuff guard: root=stuff act: answer
+  "{x:indef:cap}? I own one, somewhere. The house ate it." needs: x.countable
+  "I found {x:indef} in the couch once. Not my couch." needs: x.countable
+  "{x:cap}? The gift shop sells that. With a little turkey on it."
+  "{x:cap}? I traded mine for a biscuit. Good biscuit, no regrets."
+@rule core.ask_about.describe guard: root=describe act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? That's a word, all right. I've used it in a sentence."
+  "{x:cap}? People say that about me. I've never asked why."
+  "{x:cap}. Good word. I'd put it on a sign."
+@rule core.ask_about.house2 guard: root=house act: answer
+  "{x:indef:cap} ties a room together. Mine ties me to the room." needs: x.countable
+  "{x:cap}? Plus two cozy. Minus one if it's haunted."
+  "I moved {x:def} one pixel left. The rating went up. Don't ask me why."
+@rule core.ask_about.lore2 guard: root=lore act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? I paused the tape on that. It's a smudge, a secret smudge."
+  "{x:cap}? Everybody has a theory. Mine has string on it."
+  "They don't put {x} on the tour. I asked. The guide went quiet."
+@rule core.ask_about.hellvile2 guard: root=hellvile act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? That's a downstairs thing. Lovely people, warm, too warm."
+  "{x:cap}? You get used to it. Then you get a fan."
+@rule core.ask_about.fear2 guard: fears_topic act: opine_neg
+  "{x:cap}? Don't. I can hear my heart packing a bag."
+  "{x:cap}?! I sleep with the light on. And the other light."
+  "Not {x}, anything but {x}. I'll talk about taxes. I'll DO taxes." guard: !kid_speaker
+@rule core.ask_about.likes2 guard: likes_topic act: opine_pos
+  "{x:cap}! Who told you? I have a shelf for {x.it}, a big shelf."
+  "{x:cap}? Oh, we're doing this. Cancel your afternoon."
+  "I could talk about {x:pl} all day. I have. They asked me to stop."
+
+# ---- ASK_ABOUT(x), by voice ---------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_about.voice guard: topic act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? What a lovely thing to ask. Now, where to start?" guard: polite
+  "{x:cap}? It's {x:indef}. What else do you want, a parade?" guard: blunt needs: x.countable
+  "{x:cap}? You're asking me? Bold, wrong, but bold." guard: blunt
+  "{x:cap}. Yes. That exists." guard: flat
+  "{x:cap}. I have a feeling about {x.it}. It's a small one." guard: flat
+  "{x:up}! I have SO much to say! Hold my hat!" guard: loud
+  "{x:cap}? That's a serious subject. I'll need my serious chair." guard: serious
+  "{x:cap}? Eh, it'll sort itself out. Things do." guard: easygoing
+  "{x:cap}? I asked my left shoe. It says maybe." guard: quirky
+  "{x:cap}? Purple. That's all I'm getting, a strong purple." guard: quirky
+  "{x:cap}? Yes, no, maybe, next. I've got a thing at three." guard: quick
+  "{x:cap}... Give me a minute. {.}Give me several." guard: slow
+  "{x:cap}? In my day we had one, and we shared it. Uphill." guard: elder
+  "{x:cap}? Oh, I remember when that was new. So was I." guard: elder
+  "{x:cap}? I guess, whatever, it's fine. Why, what did you hear?" guard: teen
+  "{x:cap}? Nobody says it like that any more. But okay." guard: teen
+  "{x:cap}? We have that downstairs. Ours is on fire, so it's nicer." guard: hellborn
+  "{x:cap}? I knew about that when I was alive. Less now." guard: ghost
+  "{x:cap}? At this hour? I only know things in the daytime." guard: night
+  "{x:cap}? We just met. That's a second-visit question." guard: rel=stranger
+  "{x:cap}? For you, the long answer. Get comfy." guard: rel=best
+  "{x:cap}? Why, so you can use it against me? {.}Fine, listen." guard: rel=rival
+@rule core.ask_about.kid2 guard: kid_speaker&topic tags: kid act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? My teacher told us about that! I forgot it, but it was good."
+  "I drew {x:indef} once. Everybody said it was a dog."
+  "{x:cap}? I know a secret about {x.it}. It's that I don't know."
+  "Is {x} the one with the wheels? No? Then I don't know."
+  "{x:cap}! Can we get one? Can we get TWO?" needs: x.countable
+  "I asked a grown-up about {x}. They said 'later'. It's later now."
+
+# ---- ASK_ABOUT(x), by persona type --------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_about.type guard: topic act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? I read about {x.it}. Well, the back of the book." guard: type=quiet_bookworm
+  "{x:cap}... There's a footnote on that. I'd have to whisper it." guard: type=quiet_bookworm
+  "{x:cap}? Sounds tiring. Give me the short version and I'll nap on it." guard: type=cozy_napper
+  "{x:cap}? I'd look into it, but the blanket has me." guard: type=cozy_napper
+  "{x:cap}? Bah. It was better before, everything was." guard: type=grumpy_gremlin
+  "{x:cap}? Don't get me started. {.}Too late, I've started." guard: type=grumpy_gremlin
+  "{x:cap}. It's there, I'm here. That's the whole relationship." guard: type=deadpan_drifter
+  "{x:cap}? Saw it once, passing through. Kept passing." guard: type=deadpan_drifter
+  "{x:cap}? I think about {x.it} when the clouds go pink." guard: type=gentle_dreamer
+  "{x:cap}... That's a soft word. I'd like to float in it." guard: type=gentle_dreamer
+  "{x:cap}? Oh, I just think that's lovely! Is it lovely?" guard: type=sweet_sunbeam
+  "{x:cap}! I made a sticker chart for that. Everyone gets a sticker." guard: type=sweet_sunbeam
+  "{x:cap}! The very word is a curtain rising. On ME." guard: type=dramatic_poet
+  "Alas, {x}. I have wept over less. I have wept over toast." guard: type=dramatic_poet
+  "{x:cap}? I'm an expert. Ask anyone I've told." guard: type=cheeky_charmer
+  "{x:cap}? I'd tell you, but you'd only be impressed." guard: type=cheeky_charmer
+  "{x:cap}? I have a checklist for that. Item one: find the checklist." guard: type=diligent_helper
+  "{x:cap}? Leave it with me. I'll have a report by Thursday." guard: type=diligent_helper
+  "{x:cap}? Seen it up a mountain once. No worries either way." guard: type=chill_adventurer
+  "{x:cap}? Sure. Bring a rope and a snack, that covers most things." guard: type=chill_adventurer
+  "{x:cap}? There are rules about that. Three, and I wrote all three." guard: type=stern_captain
+  "{x:cap}. Stand up straight when you ask about {x.it}." guard: type=stern_captain
+  "{x:cap}? Flip a coin. Heads I know, tails I make it up." guard: type=wild_card
+  "{x:cap}? I bet a hat on that once. Notice I'm not wearing a hat." guard: type=wild_card
+  "{x:cap}? I've got a five-step plan for that. Step one: more steps." guard: type=eager_go_getter
+  "{x:cap}? Great question. I'm adding it to my goals, all of them." guard: type=eager_go_getter
+  "{x:cap}! Ooh, does it come in glitter? It should!" guard: type=bubbly_sparkler
+  "{x:cap}? Yay! I don't know what we're doing, but yay!" guard: type=bubbly_sparkler
+  "{x:cap}? Right, everyone listen up. I'll say this once, maybe twice." guard: type=fiery_leader
+  "{x:cap}! Good. We move on {x.it} at dawn, so bring snacks." guard: type=fiery_leader
+  "{x:cap}? What if we took it apart? I have a spoon." guard: type=chaos_goblin
+  "{x:cap}? Hee, I hid one of those. I won't say where, because I forgot." guard: type=chaos_goblin
+
+# ---- ASK_OPINION(x), by stance ----------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_opinion.pro2 guard: stance=pro act: opine_pos
+  "{x:cap}? {ask.star.pro} Next question."
+  "I like {x:pl} {ask.more}. There, I said it."
+  "My opinion of {x:pl}? High. Embarrassingly high."
+  "{x:def:cap} {x.is} {x.good}. That's my opinion and I'm framing it."
+  "{x:cap}? I'm for {x.it}. I'd wear the badge, I'd make the badge."
+  "I think {x:pl} never let me down. People have. Chairs have."
+  "{x:cap}? Yes. Easy, ask me a hard one."
+  "Honestly? I think about {x:pl} more than is normal. Fondly."
+  "{x:cap} gets my vote. I vote early. I vote with a flag."
+  "If {x:pl} ran for Mayor, I'd knock on doors."
+  "{x:cap}? Good. {x.good:cap}, even, and I don't say that lightly."
+  "I'd give {x:pl} a trophy. A real one. With a tiny me on top."
+@rule core.ask_opinion.con2 guard: stance=con act: opine_neg
+  "{x:cap}? {ask.star.con} Next question."
+  "I like {x:pl} {ask.less}. There, I said it."
+  "My opinion of {x:pl}? Low. You'd need a shovel."
+  "{x:def:cap} {x.is} {x.bad}. That's my opinion and I'm laminating it."
+  "{x:cap}? Against. I'd sign a thing, I'd start the thing."
+  "I think {x:pl} let me down once. I don't forget. I have a book."
+  "{x:cap}? Not for me. For somebody, maybe, somebody far away."
+  "Do you want the polite answer on {x:pl}? I don't have one."
+  "{x:cap} lost my vote. Then found it. Then lost it again."
+  "If {x:pl} ran for Mayor, I'd move. I'd take the house."
+  "{x:cap}? Bad. {x.bad:cap}, even, and I'm in a good mood."
+  "I think {x:pl} peaked early. Before I got there."
+@rule core.ask_opinion.neutral2 guard: stance=neutral act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? {ask.star.mid} Don't make me pick a side."
+  "I've got half an opinion on {x:pl}. Want the top half?"
+  "{x:cap}? I'm waiting for more reviews to come in."
+  "{x:def:cap} {x.is} {x.adj}. Past that, I plead the nap."
+  "What do I think of {x:pl}? Rarely. I rarely think of {x:pl}."
+  "{x:cap}? I can see both sides. I'm standing on neither."
+  "My opinion of {x:pl} is on order. Six to eight weeks."
+  "{x:cap}? Some days yes, some days no. Today is a some day."
+  "I'd vote 'present' on {x:pl}. Then I'd go home."
+  "{x:cap}? Fine. That's the word, and I looked for a better one."
+  "I thought about {x:pl} once. Nothing came of it."
+@rule core.ask_opinion.joke guard: topic act: joke
+  "My opinion on {x:pl} costs one biscuit. {.}I'll wait."
+  "{x:cap}? I have opinions on everything. Most are about soup."
+  "You want my take on {x:pl}? I left it at the Buffet."
+  "{x:cap}? I'd tell you, but I charge by the word. That's eleven."
+@rule core.ask_opinion.pass guard: topic act: dismiss
+  "{x:cap}? No comment. I've been burned before, by the Mayor."
+  "I keep my opinions on {x:pl} to myself. And one duck."
+  "Opinions? In front of everyone? What is this, a town meeting?"
+@rule core.ask_opinion.swerve act: change_topic
+  "I'd rather give you my opinion on {like:pl}. It's longer."
+  "Skip that. Ask what I think of {like:pl}. Go on, ask."
+  "No opinion. But on {like:pl}? Sit down."
+@rule core.ask_opinion.likes guard: likes_topic act: opine_pos
+  "{x:cap}? You're asking the president of the fan club. And the treasurer."
+  "My opinion of {x:pl}? I have the tattoo. It's a drawing, but still."
+@rule core.ask_opinion.hates guard: hates_topic act: opine_neg
+  "{x:cap}? I'd rather eat the plate."
+  "You know how I feel about {x}. The whole street knows."
+@rule core.ask_opinion.fears guard: fears_topic act: opine_neg
+  "My opinion of {x:pl}? From far away. Behind a door."
+  "{x:cap}? Let {x.it} stay far away. I'll stay here, behind a door."
+
+# ---- the comparison sub-rules: "I like pies {ask.more}." --------------------------------------
+@rule ask.more
+  "more than soup"
+  "more than naps"
+  "more than my own porch"
+  "more than a day off"
+  "more than is healthy"
+  "more than the Mayor likes hats"
+@rule ask.less
+  "less than wet socks"
+  "less than Mondays"
+  "less than the fog"
+  "less than a cold bath"
+  "less than a queue"
+  "less than soup with a hair in it"
+
+# ---- ASK_OPINION(x), by what the topic is -----------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_opinion.root_pos guard: topic act: opine_pos
+  "{x:cap}? Tasty. I judge all food on one question: is there more?" guard: root=food&stance=pro
+  "{x:def:cap}? Lovely spot. I'd live there if my house would let me." guard: root=places&stance=pro
